  "notes": "The Dipset entry that is brighter than the other two: major-key gospel/soul flips weighted over triumphal minor, an open chord voicing for the horn/organ fanfares, and the highest `countermelody.densityRatio` of the three because the hooks are gang chants doubling the top line — an octave-echo counter is literally what a chant doubling a melody is, so `octave_echo` carries weight 4. The 16th kick pickups are `syncopation` 0.42 with `tresilloBias` 0.12 against the 1-and-3& anchor, and the crashes on section changes are a `crash` perc lane. ⚠ The I–IV and i–VII families at weight 2 are REDUCTIONS of the researched I–IV–V and i–VI–VII, not separately researched claims. ⚠ `medium`, and the research names its own inferred parameter: the idiom is documented at producer level but the artist-level tempo is catalog-level, so the 92–102 band and its 97 centre are the least-supported numbers in this file.",
